// The standard library's own tests, written in Wip. The
// library is compiled into the compiler, so its tests cannot live beside
// it, in `std/`, without shipping in every program: they live here, in a
// module of their own, and reach the library as a program does — through
// what it exports.
//
// `wip test tests/std/main.wip` runs them, and `verify.sh` does that too.
// The file itself holds nothing: the tests are in the `.test.wip` files
// beside it.
